.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CHAIN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-chain
.Nd check an append-only chain of capsules
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis chain
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl -anchor Ar der-file ...
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Ar dir ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A chain is a log of capsules to which a link is only ever added.
Start it by sealing the first in format 2, and add each next one with
the last as its only input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis seal --format 2 -k me log/1
$ noqtis seal -k me --input prev=log/1 log/2
$ noqtis seal -k me --input prev=log/2 log/3
.Ed
.Pp
The seal of each link then signs the id of the one before, so a link
cannot be changed, removed or put in another place without the chain
failing.
.Nm noqtis chain
checks the folders
.Ar dir ,
oldest first: each link checks
.Po
as
.Xr noqtis-check 1
with
.Fl p
and
.Fl -anchor
.Pc ,
each after the first names exactly the one before it as its only input
(a fork, a gap or links out of order fail), and every link is sealed by
the same key.
The first link's own inputs are not followed, so a chain can be checked
from any link on.
The last row is the chain's head: the last link's id
.Pq Xr nqcapid 3 ,
which a reader can keep or publish to notice a chain cut back later.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub
The key every link must be sealed by.
Without it, the first link's own key is trusted, and a note says so.
.It Fl -anchor Ar der-file
A TSA root or issuing certificate (DER), up to 32, for timestamped
seals.
.It Fl j , Fl -json
The rows as JSON.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The chain checks.
.It 1
A link does not check, does not follow the one before it, or is sealed
by another key.
.It 2
A usage error, or a folder that is not there.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqdchain 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
